Shared Pupu24 + KDA4 S0a source attribution

The Pupu encoder adapter reconstructs inference operations from PupuM2D
(sizigi/PupuM2D, MIT) and historical timm EVA, AttentionRope, RoPE and SwiGLU
implementations (huggingface/pytorch-image-models v1.0.22, Apache-2.0).
The Slaney mel-filter routine follows librosa 0.11.0 (ISC).
Their original license texts are retained in LICENSES/.

Modified behavior includes a dependency-light encoder without the predictor or
masking branch, strict EMA-teacher subset loading, preserved unpooled 2D audio
tokens, and shared audio/event execution with new interleaved KDA blocks.

The KDA reference is an independent PyTorch implementation of the published
Kimi Delta Attention recurrence and parameterization. Primary sources and
engineering differences are documented in ARCHITECTURE.md. Optional fla-core
is installed separately under its own license; its source is not vendored.

No pretrained weights, chart or audio bytes are distributed here. Code licenses
